  "cut_point": "We are given a basketball training scenario with **three players** (let's call them A, B, and C) who are passing the ball in a **cycle**. The **rules** are:\n\n- Each player must **pass the ball to another teammate** after receiving it.\n- The **first player** (say A) makes the **first pass**.\n- We are to find how many ways the **first player (A)** can **receive the ball for the fifth time** just in time to make a **layup**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understand the Process\n\n- There are **3 players**: A, B, C\n- The ball starts with **A**\n- At each step, the **current player** must **pass to one of the other two** players\n- We are to find the number of **distinct sequences of passes** such that **A receives the ball for the 5th time** on the **5th pass** (i.e., at the end of the 5th pass, A gets the ball for the 5th time)",
